+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates model-supplied tool input against the tool's registered JSON Schema before invoking its executor. This makes a malformed call a recoverable tool result inside the bounded conversation loop.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names a missing required property, does not invoke the executor for that call, and lets the provider correct the input on the next round. ([validated by: returns a missing-location error to the model and lets it retry within the tool loop](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L22))
+- Rejections for wrong types or enum values name the failing property path and constraint in returned text and log lines without exposing the rejected value, and do not invoke the executor. ([validated by: rejects wrong types and enum values with path-only messages and logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L76))
+- A static tool's schema is compiled at registration and retained across calls; valid input, including unknown properties, reaches the executor unchanged, without default insertion or type coercion. ([validated by: uses one registered static schema across ten calls while passing valid extra keys unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L121))
+- An invalid static schema throws during registration with the tool name in the error, while an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` from `execute`. ([validated by: fails registration for an invalid schema and keeps unknown-tool errors as throws](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L147))
+- A function-valued definition resolves its schema for each call and validates against that call's resolved schema, caching a compiled validator by schema object when the object is reused. ([validated by: validates each function-valued definition against the schema returned for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L155))
